# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and adjust for this machine. Every key is optional.

# Where papers, reports, notes and study records live. Default: this app folder
# (paper folders there are git-ignored). Use a separate disk for large libraries.
# PAPERLAB_DATA_DIR=D:\PaperLab\data

# Offline selection translation (划词翻译). Defaults point into ./models/ (git-ignored):
#   dictionary : ECDICT index built by  scripts/build_dictionary.py <ecdict.csv> <ecdict.db>
#   model      : Tencent Hy-MT2 GGUF (Apache-2.0), e.g. Hy-MT2-7B-Q4_K_M.gguf (4.6 GB, fits 8 GB VRAM)
#                or Hy-MT2-1.8B-Q4_K_M.gguf (1.1 GB, also fine on CPU)
#   server     : llama-server.exe from a llama.cpp release (CUDA build for NVIDIA GPUs)
# PAPERLAB_DICTIONARY=models\ecdict.db
# PAPERLAB_MT_MODEL=models\Hy-MT2-7B-Q4_K_M.gguf
# PAPERLAB_LLAMA_SERVER=models\llama.cpp\llama-server.exe
# Layers offloaded to the GPU; 0 runs on CPU only (slow for the 7B model).
# PAPERLAB_MT_GPU_LAYERS=99

# Papers whose analysis you keep with GPT; web Codex jobs will not rewrite them.
# PAPERLAB_GPT_AUTHORED=local-0123456789abcdef0123,2410.24164

# The name in the library greeting goes in frontend/.env.local (read at build time):
#   VITE_PAPERLAB_USER_NAME=YourName
